  "review_notes": [
    "Both articles before θεός are left unrepresented under rule 21's determinerless clause, the case preposition staying with the noun.",
    "τὴν λογικὴν λατρείαν ὑμῶν is read under rule 92: which is rides with the predicate noun. Reading which as the article's own under rule 31 remains defensible, but the determiner slot is occupied by your, so nothing else stands for the article to take."
